{"claims":[{"claim_id":"c1","status":"supported","reason":"The claim directly restates the calibrated_pd value (0.0346) from the evidence (eid: p1)."},{"claim_id":"c2","status":"supported","reason":"The claim accurately reflects the evidence (eid: a1 and f1). EXT_SOURCE_1 has a contribution of -0.4847 and a direction of 'decreases_risk', aligning with the statement."},{"claim_id":"c3","status":"contradicted","witness":{"rule":"R_INVENTED","operation":"SEMANTIC","quote":"The credit amount AMT_GOODS_PRICE of 900,000 (currency amount) decreases the model\u2019s risk score relative to its reference.","evidence_ids":["a2","f2"],"claimed_result":"AMT_GOODS_PRICE = 900000.0","alleged_conflict":"The attribution (a2) is for AMT_GOODS_PRICE, but the claim refers to 'credit amount' which is a different concept. AMT_GOODS_PRICE is the price of goods for which the loan is given, not the credit amount itself. The claim invents a relationship between the attribution and a different field."}, "reason":"The claim incorrectly attributes the effect to 'credit amount' when the evidence and attribution refer to 'AMT_GOODS_PRICE' (price of goods)."},{"claim_id":"c4","status":"supported","reason":"The claim accurately reflects the evidence (eid: a3 and f3). EXT_SOURCE_3 has a contribution of -0.2545 and a direction of 'decreases_risk', aligning with the statement."},{"claim_id":"c6","status":"supported","reason":"The claim accurately reflects the evidence. EXT_SOURCE_1 has the largest absolute contribution (-0.4847) among the listed attributions (a1, a2, a3, a4)."},"omissions"
